WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.768
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.868
We're here with Michael Shannon.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.537
And, Michael,
this is very exciting --

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.773
your brother and your mother

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.308
are here in the audience
with us tonight.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.542
-Oh, they are?
-Yeah.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.010
-What?
Shut the front door.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.278
[ Cheering and applause ]
-There they are,
right over there.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.446
-What?

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.580
Oh, my God!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.615
Look at that.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.650
There's Geraldine
and there's David.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.487
-Geraldine and David.
And David--

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.255
David's 40th birthday today.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.124
-Yeah, my little brother,
he's 40 years old today.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.725
-Yeah, that's great.
-January 3rd.

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:27.526
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:28.894
Congratulations, Dave.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.030
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.333
-Okay.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.001
-Can we do anything for him?

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.102
-What would you like to do?

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.403
-I don't know.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.671
[ Laughter ]
Do you want to --

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.372
You want to come --
Why don't you come up?

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:41.941
-No.
-Oh, come on!

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.810
[ Cheering and applause ]
Come on, come up, come up.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.478
Come on, man.

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:47.414
Get on up here.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.316
[ Whistling ]

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:57.490
Yeah, man.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.493
Oh, man.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.627
Alright.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:02.962
Happy Birthday, bro.
-Hey. Thanks, Mike.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.665
-Happy Birthday.
-Hey. Thanks.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.932
-Have a seat.

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.735
-Wow. Okay.
-Now we should stress

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.637
if it was your mom's birthday,
you would've brought her up?

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:12.538
-No. Still him.
-Okay.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.040
[ Laughter ]
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.341
-Alright, so, Dave, I did know
this was going to happen...

00:01:16.341 --> 00:01:17.676
-Oh!
-Oh, gosh.

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:18.745
-...we met each other backstage

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:19.945
-We did.
-and I think I prayed it --

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.481
I played it -- excuse me --
pretty cool.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.683
-Yeah, you did.
-So, hey, you guys,

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.518
this is Dave's birthday.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.787
Alright, you want to blow
that out for us real quick?

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.855
-Yeah.
-No, we're not going
to do the song.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.323
-Yeah, no singing.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.090
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.024
-Alright.
-[ Blows ]

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:32.825
-Nice!
-Alright, there we go.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.160
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.228
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.230
-Alright, so, Dave,
we mentioned --

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.799
we mentioned Kentucky.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.267
-Yeah.
-That's where you guys grew up
and you still live there.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.269
What was it like
growing up together?

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.871
Did you guys get along as kids?

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:45.971
-I think so.

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:47.873
[ Laughter ]
As far as I can remember.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.043
-We used to play
this game called Bonkers.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.111
-Yeah.
-Remember this game?

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.811
-I remember Bonkers, yes.
-So we had --

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:54.280
-Unfortunately.
-Yeah. It was a hallway

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.116
[ Laughter ]
where all the bedroom --

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.017
there were like
three bedroom doors.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.119
And what you'd have to do is
you'd have to --

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.955
Because we have two sisters,
so there were four of us.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.624
So, one of us would be stationed
in each of the doors

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:07.893
and then one of us would have
to run down the hall.

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:09.262
-I got to be the runner.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.330
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. You were
usually the runner

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.664
because you were the little one.
-Right.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.699
-And so, everybody
in the doorway had a pillow

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:15.234
and you had to try
and run down the hall

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.503
without getting
completely creamed
-Beat the hell out of me.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.373
[ Laughter ]
-by a pillow.
-I mean cream me, you know.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.575
-Bonkers is an excellent name
for that game.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.210
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, Bonkers, yeah.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.745
-Obviously, your brother is
an accomplished bongo player.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.447
-Right.
-Did you have
a musical upbringing?

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:29.982
Did you play anything?
-Drums.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.384
-I grew up playing -- I actually
started playing the cello

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:33.820
and then now, I play the drums.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.421
-Alright, still play the drums.
-Still play the drums.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.856
-Alright. There you go.
Did you guys --

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.691
Were you the kind of family --
Did you take a lot of road trips

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.459
as kids?

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:41.960
[ Laughter ]
-No. Where did we go?
-No.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.163
-We'd go to the Natural Bridge
every once in a while.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.764
-Yeah.
-What's the Natural Bridge?

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:47.467
-Oh, it's beautiful.
It's in Kentucky.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.269
It's in the Red River Gorge.
-Red River Gorge.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:53.339
Yeah.
-It's a natural bridge that,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.908
I guess, was just made by time.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.877
[ Laughter ]
Eroding rocks.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.812
-Yeah.
-Very well named.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.347
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.148
-It's a rock.
-It's not false advertising.

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:04.984
[ Laughter ]
-When you get there,
you're not like,

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.819
"This isn't natural."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.987
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, it's Styrofoam.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.255
[ Laughter ]
They painted it."

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.990
So, wait, now, Dave,
growing up with Michael,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.794
did you have any sense that
his path would be into acting?

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:18.464
-I mean, yeah, I guess so.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.932
I guess you could say that,
yeah.

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.968
I mean, I always knew there was
something special about him.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.036
-Oh, that's very sweet, yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:26.706
[ Awws ]
-What's your least favorite
of his movies?

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.375
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.
-There you go.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.312
-"8 Mile."
-Oh, there you go. Interesting.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.279
[ Laughter ]
-"8 Mile."
-Don't hear that very often.

00:03:34.279 --> 00:03:37.550
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yep.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.285
-I know this T-shirt
looks very threatening,

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:43.556
but we got this at a a duckpin
bowling place in Cincinnati.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.458
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Alright, got it.
-Because I was just shooting

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.759
something in Cincinnati

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.494
and they came up to visit me
one weekend

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.397
and this is --
-Pins Mechanical Co.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.398
-Cincinnati.
-Actually, that's very helpful

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.899
because it is very menacing

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:55.367
and it's kind of the opposite,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.436
which is it's bowling,
but with the tiny pins.

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.138
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, with the tiny pins.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.908
-And it's not about force.
It's about finesse.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.943
[ Laughter ]
Because Mom won.
-Yeah, she won.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.379
We played her.
-Can't beat her.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.547
-Geraldine, were you surprised
you won bowling,

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:09.615
or did you expect it?

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:10.850
-I expected it.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.051
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:15.020
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.591
-Alright, so, Michael, you know,
I don't want to --

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.926
I know you're the guest
on the show,

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.194
but we're celebrating
your brother,

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.495
so, why don't you tell us
what's your favorite thing

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.130
about your brother Dave here
on his 40th birthday?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.531
-Oh, man.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.066
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.268
-My brother's one of the
toughest people I know.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:30.403
-Oh, right?
-Yeah.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.171
-Cool.
-He's been through a lot

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.607
and he's still here
to tell the tale, so.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.341
-That's right.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.375
-Yep.
-Yep!

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:37.910
-That's my brother.
-Well...

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.045
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:41.080
...thank you very much
for being here.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.284
Thank you for being
our second guest of 2023.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.485
-Right, yeah.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:48.921
-You guys, give it up
for the Shannon Brothers!

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.690
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.426
The finale of "George &amp; Tammy"
airs January 8th on Showtime.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.060
We'll be right back
with Danielle Brooks.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.763
Happy birthday, Dave.

